# Additional environment variables for SilverBullet, read by the systemd unit
# after $install_dir/default.env. This file is preserved across upgrades and
# is yours to edit.
#
# Supported (see https://silverbullet.md/HTTP%20API and the upstream
# Install/Configuration docs):
#
#   SB_AUTH_TOKEN   Bearer token for the HTTP API. Since 2.11, an install that
#                   went through the setup wizard stores its accounts in
#                   users.json, and creating an API token from the dashboard is
#                   the supported way to authenticate API calls. Do NOT set
#                   SB_USER or SB_AUTH_TOKEN on such an install.
#   SB_HTTP_LOGGING set to any value to enable HTTP request logging
#   SB_FS_WATCH     auto (default) | poll | off - see the upstream docs if the
#                   space lives on a network mount (NFS/SMB)
#
# WARNING - SB_USER and SB_AUTH_TOKEN prevent SilverBullet from starting once
# the install has been through the setup wizard. The server refuses to boot with:
#
#   this folder contains spaces.json (multi-space config) but SB_USER is set.
#   Accounts now live in users.json - unset SB_USER
#
# The legacy advice floating around in issue #18 (add SB_USER + SB_AUTH_TOKEN
# to this file, and set the app public) was correct for the single-space mode
# SilverBullet used before 2.11. On a current install it either pins the server
# to the deprecated single-space mode, or - if the setup wizard has already run -
# stops it from booting at all. See doc/POST_UPGRADE.d/2.11.1~ynh1.md.